This packaging is adapted from Debian's SaunaFS 5.8.0-1.1 package:
https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/s/saunafs/saunafs_5.8.0-1.1.debian.tar.xz
Packaging repository: https://salsa.debian.org/hpc-team/saunafs

The original debian/copyright and changelog history are retained. Debian's
packaging is GPL-3.0-or-later; see the debian/* stanza in debian/copyright.

LeilFS adaptations:
* Package roles follow rpm/leilfs.spec, with client-dev as Debian's name for
  client-devel. The former common account setup lives in leilfs-user.
* CGI assets and the standalone web server are separate packages.
* Current names and legacy aliases are both included in explicit manifests.
* All files staged by CMake must be accounted for (dh_missing --fail-missing).
* Runtime client libraries are retained in leilfs-client, because the static
  client code can dlopen the mount helper. The RPM spec currently discards these.
* Version metadata, paths, compiler options and dependencies match this checkout.
* LTO is disabled: LTO links fail with undefined C++ string references in
  richacl_string.cc; the same fat archive objects link successfully without LTO.
  Debian hardening remains enabled.
* No gtest source copying, historical source patches, legacy SysV scripts,
  source-download targets or Debian-maintainer VCS metadata are imported.
* Services are not enabled or started on initial install. Upgrades keep them
  running during unpacking and restart previously running services afterward.
  Removal/deconfiguration stops services through deb-systemd-invoke.
* The service account and persistent data survive purge, unlike the original
  common package script, which deleted the account.
* Active configuration is installed as conffiles. Initial exports deny all
  clients and the HTTP monitor binds to localhost until configured.

The CMake build is shared with RPM. Debian builds use debhelper rather than
CPack. No Debian source patches are applied to the current upstream checkout.
